   {
    "primary": {
     "title": [
      {
       "type": "heading2",
       "text": "Icon system",
       "spans": []
      }
     ],
     "ingress_title": [],
     "body": [
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "text": "The icons are provided as a font file, which is the most convenient way to use them on most platforms. However, they can also be used as vector graphics files if necessary.",
       "spans": [],
       "direction": "ltr"
      },
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "text": "You can download the icons on the For designers page.",
       "spans": [
        {
         "start": 34,
         "end": 52,
         "type": "hyperlink",
         "data": {
          "id": "ZGdbnhAAACAAevFi",
          "type": "design_system_content",
          "tags": [
           "ds"
          ],
          "lang": "en-eu",
          "slug": "for-designers",
          "first_publication_date": "2023-05-19T11:22:35+0000",
          "last_publication_date": "2024-06-10T11:01:19+0000",
          "uid": "_ds_for-designers",
          "link_type": "Document",
          "isBroken": false
         }
        }
       ],
       "direction": "ltr"
      },
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "text": "Icons are named by describing what can be seen to make them use-case agnostic. There are a few exceptions, like play or copy that would be unnecessarily hard to find when named otherwise.",
       "spans": [
        {
         "start": 112,
         "end": 116,
         "type": "em"
        },
        {
         "start": 120,
         "end": 124,
         "type": "em"
        }
       ],
       "direction": "ltr"
      },
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "text": "Icon name can include three parts:\n- Token type, in this case icon\n- Form, that describes the dominant shape of the icon\n- Descriptor, that works as a cue for the visual presentation\nFor example the general check mark icon is named icon-check-mark. The icon where a check mark is enclosed in a circle is icon-circle-check-mark.",
       "spans": [
        {
         "start": 232,
         "end": 247,
         "type": "em"
        },
        {
         "start": 304,
         "end": 326,
         "type": "em"
        }
       ],
       "direction": "ltr"
      }
